This licence covers what is actually ours in this repository: the setup
script, the tools, the analysis summaries and the documentation. It does NOT
cover The Movies itself.

The Movies and The Movies: Stunts & Effects are (c) 2005-2006 Lionhead
Studios / Activision, and are not ours to license. Their executables, data,
movies, music and art are not in this repository and are excluded by
.gitignore.

Two consequences worth being explicit about:

  * You need your own copy of the game to use any of this. Setup.cmd copies
    your install into game/; the pipeline reads it from there.

  * Unpacked and lifted code is a derivative work of the binary it came from.
    Anything this pipeline emits into work/ or src/recomp/gen/ carries whatever
    licence the original carries, not this one. The MIT grant above stops at
    our own work.
